	(text "level shifting: 2x SN74CBTD3861 bus switches, Amiga side on A, RP2350 side on B"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 466.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.0 3.0)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7bce75fe-a830-5fd9-ae04-09b1906114e4")
	)
	(text "VCC = AMIGA_5V_FUSED: the diode-dropped gate limits the B side to ~2.6-3.0 V typ (TI fig. 2) and the RP2350 internal pull-up completes the rise to 3.3 V. OE tied low (always on). Keep VCC >= 4.5 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 474.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "91e3cbc9-9eb2-5059-b96b-7c36c8979f26")
	)
	(text "F1 is fitted: this rail is the switch supply. Cabling only the DE9 ports to a running Amiga leaves the rail dead and the port pull-ups drag the lines low - connect the keyboard cable or USB-C first (as rev6)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 477.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "83893a02-8ee3-58f7-b55c-978f218735db")
	)
	(text "With the Amiga off the switches are open and the B side floats: firmware enables the RP2350 internal pull-ups on every _lo input."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 481.42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b752c9a7-4420-5ef6-aeba-c6450b0f61ca")
	)
	(text "Amiga-side pull-ups: 19 x 10k to AMIGA_5V_FUSED in 4-element arrays (RN5 element 4 spare). ESD clamps D10-D28 on every Amiga-facing line."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 484.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0689c5db-98c1-5129-8cbb-a084df176dce")
	)
